B.bWx=new A.cJ("cards","An elegant, expandable card view of a table's rows.",B.baC,!1)
B.caO=new A.t("segments",B.Z,"List of { label, child } segments.",B.e,null)
B.c4u=new A.t("fill",B.W,'Fill the (bounded) parent and hand the active tab the remaining height via Expanded \u2014 needed when a tab hosts a height-filling surface (a bubl board, notepad, nested explorer, or a map/table/chart asking for height:"fill"). The active tab also republishes its own bounded height, so a height:"fill" child fills the TAB exactly (not the whole body) and pans internally. As a ROOT body it also takes the exact viewport height instead of the page-scroll fallback. Default off: segments shrink-wrap and drop into a scroll view.',B.e,null)
B.cgn=new A.t("chips",B.W,"Render the header as a compact row of small icon chips instead of full FilledButton text pills. Each segment map may carry an `icon` (a nav icon-name string, same registry as tab-bar icons); without one the chip falls back to the label's first letter in a small circle. The active chip is tinted, inactive chips are faint, and the current segment's label is shown next to the strip. Default off: the classic text-pill header (byte-identical to before this key existed).",B.e,null)
B.c7B=new A.t("swipe",B.W,"With `chips:true`, a horizontal drag ANYWHERE ON THE CHIP STRIP (never the body) advances/retreats the active segment, with an animated slide transition. Deliberately scoped to the strip \u2014 never a body-wide PageView \u2014 so a one-finger drag inside the active tab (a bubl board drag/marquee, an outline scroll, a canvas pan) is never intercepted. Default off.",B.e,null)
