B.c6O=new A.t("dataLinkColumn",B.x,"Data overlay: id of the step row (in `nodesTable`) a data row feeds. When set, a light PAINTED-ONLY line is drawn from the data node to that step \u2014 no row is written to `edgesTable`, so a deleted step just makes the line vanish, never an orphaned edge.",B.e,null)
B.c85=new A.t("filter",B.Z,"Opt-in row scope for `nodesTable` (and, unless `dataFilter` overrides it, `dataTable` too) \u2014 same shape as `bubl`'s filter: {column, value} or {column, in:[...]}; `value`/each `in` entry may be a token ($selected:<table>, $rowId, $playerId). Absent = all rows (unchanged behavior); resolved value/set EMPTY = no rows, never all. A node/data row freshly created while a resolved scalar {column, value} filter is scoping the view is stamped with that column:value so it stays in scope.",B.e,null)
B.aeT=new A.t("dataFilter",B.Z,"Opt-in override of `filter` for `dataTable` only, when the data table scopes on a different column than `nodesTable`. Same shape as `filter`. Absent = `dataTable` falls back to `filter`.",B.e,null)
B.afg=new A.t("scopeColumn",B.x,"Opt-in ENGINE scope filter for `nodesTable` \u2014 the same convention the `explorer` node's `scopeColumn` reads via `activeScope`, so a canvas bound to a scoped table (e.g. a File > Board > nodes chain) shows only the open file/board's nodes even when no ancestor explorer for that hop happened to mount. Distinct from `filter` (a token-resolved value/set filter); the two may combine. Absent = unchanged behavior.",B.e,null)
